Q2.
Suppose you play two-player game where there are two piles of 10 stones.
Let's call them pile $A$ and pile $B$.
Each player take turns to remove stones.
A player can
\begin{enumerate}
  \li Remove one stone from pile $A$.
  \li Remove two stones from pile $B$.
  \li Remove one stone from pile $B$.
  \li Move one stone from $A$ to $B$.
\end{enumerate}
Is there a winning strategy for the first or the second player?
If there's one, explain it clearly.
If there isn't explain why.

